# Translation precision for the two-detector publication

The original root note and seal are unchanged. Its copies of the exact J_-
preparation retain their A/B assignments, so their translations must preserve
the bipartition. Public text should say this explicitly. For displacement R
along a single axis, choose even R. The static plaquette covariance formula
itself is valid for integer R; the physical two-preparation construction and
its large-separation diagonal may use the even subsequence. All executed
spatial examples use even R. No effect identity, error estimate or numerical
result changes. This clarification was recorded while the independent PRE
was still blind and was not disclosed to that checker.
